  "body": "The current draft uses a promise-returning `read()` method to get the data. @isaacs outlined a different paradigm at http://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-webapps/2013JulSep/0355.html, which you should read through and grok. (I've renamed his \"read\" to \"readCurrentBufferSync\" to avoid confusion.)\n\nIt's a bit more awkward, but might be better and more low-level.\n\nYou can build either on top of the other; he demonstrates building promise-returning `read()` on top of the triple-API, and you can proactively call `read()` and store in a synchronously-readable buffer in order to build the triple-API on top of `read()`. However, the latter strategy imposes an end-of-microtask delay, which may not be a good idea.\n",
